# Chroma library, modern Earth: SACRED LINES (S5, v22.3, cast_want: sacred / tragic / amends).
# A line forms in a way that has led for years and twice cost them something real (line kinds: promise W, truth U,
# own_say B, loved R, home G; Outer world dynamics.json "offers"). Offer moments: sacred: <kind>, offer: money|post|favour,
# round: first|raised, slot {offer} (the Outer world's offer text, verbatim, after a colon); options line: hold|cross,
# one of each per colour. Tragic moments: two lines collide, sacred: <a>+<b>, options tragic: a|b|torn, no clean option.
# Amends moments: the line once crossed, options heal: amends|reflect|not_yet. 30 offers, 5 tragic, 10 amends.
# Per way, its one-letter option plus its cross (first letter) = 140. Spec chroma-ideas/social-mechanics.md S5.


# Chroma library, modern Earth: SACRED LINES, offers on a promise (S5 sacred lines, v22.3, DRAFT cast_want: sacred).
# The character holds a promise line (a promise kept, a fair process). The Engine fills {offer} verbatim (table_offer_W.txt).
# Every option carries line: hold | cross. Chances: per way, its one-letter option plus its cross (first letter) = 140;
# hold 55-85, cross 75-95. Syntax: header of build.py.
#   pair 1  promise + money,  1a first WU (s1)  / 1b raised BRG (s2)
#   pair 2  promise + post,   2a first WB (s3)  / 2b raised URG (s4)
#   pair 3  promise + favour, 3a first WR (s1)  / 3b raised UBG (s2)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 1: promise + money

== good money against the word you gave
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: WU
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: money, community
horizon: years
roles: friend, colleague, neighbour
cast_want: sacred
sacred: promise
offer: money
round: first
earth: a line you will not cross is put to a price: good money, if you go back on your word to the people who trust you
times: People asked to trade something they hold sacred for money often refuse outright and take offence at the offer itself (Tetlock 2003; Fiske and Tetlock 1997).
gap: 3-8
scene: For years {N} has kept {Ns} word to the people {N} works and lives beside: no money made at their cost, however lean the month. Twice that word has cost {N} dearly, and twice {N} has paid. Now, in a thin season, someone takes {N} aside one evening. The offer is put plainly: {offer}.
scene W: The word was given to people who count on it; but the family at home counts on {N} too, and the bills are real.
scene U: {N} has done the sums: what the money would cover, and what a broken word costs in the years after.
scene B: Nobody gets to buy {Ns} word, and nobody gets to tell {N} what to do with {Ns} own evenings either.
scene R: {N} sees the faces of the people the word was given to, and the faces at home who need more than {N} brings in.
scene G: The people who trust {N} are the ones {N} grew up among, and will grow old among.
- W | say no: you gave your word, and a word is not for sale | line: hold | v: conformity, benevolence | mark: kept your word | act: say no: they gave their word, and a word is not for sale | chance: 60
- U | take it: the sums say the household cannot get through the winter without it | line: cross | v: security, achievement | chance: 85
- B | refuse: your word is yours, and it is not on the market | line: hold | v: self-direction, power | act: refuse: their word is their own, and it is not on the market | chance: 65
- R | take it, for someone at home who needs the money now | line: cross | v: benevolence | chance: 85
- G | decline quietly: the people here have trusted you all your life | line: hold | v: tradition | act: decline quietly: the people here have trusted them all their life | chance: 60
- W>U | take it for one season, under a strict rule you set yourself, to pay for training | line: cross | v: security, achievement | act: take it for one season, under a strict rule they set themselves, to pay for training | chance: 80
- U>B | work out what the money would tie you to, and stay free by refusing | line: hold | v: self-direction | mark: turned down a chance | act: work out what the money would tie them to, and stay free by refusing | chance: 55
- B>R | drive a hard bargain, then spend the money on a fresh start far from here | line: cross | v: power, stimulation | chance: 75
- R>G | turn it down loudly, in front of everyone, and stand with your own people | line: hold | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: made an enemy | act: turn it down loudly, in front of everyone, and stand with their own people | chance: 55
- G>W | take it quietly, as people here do in hard years, and share it round the family | line: cross | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 80
works: The choice settles, and in time the people around {N} say they know exactly where they stand with {N}.
works: One of the old hands nods at {N} in the street, and says nothing, which says enough.
fails: It costs more than {N} expected, and a door {N} had counted on quietly closes.
fails: {N} lies awake more nights than {N} will admit, going over the evening it was offered.

