- R | take it, for a fresh start and a life that is no longer stuck | line: cross | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 85
- G | turn it down quietly, and keep to the slow, honest way up | line: hold | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 60
- W>R | accept, and use the post to look after the people you love, by the book | line: cross | v: benevolence, security | act: accept, and use the post to look after the people they love, by the book | chance: 80
- U>G | think it through, see what it would cost your name at home, and decline | line: hold | v: tradition, self-direction | act: think it through, see what it would cost their name at home, and decline | chance: 55
- B>W | accept, but bargain hard for a say in how things are run, to make it fairer | line: cross | v: power, universalism | chance: 75
- R>U | say no on the spot, then tell the people you promised exactly what was offered | line: hold | v: self-direction, universalism | act: say no on the spot, then tell the people they promised exactly what was offered | chance: 55
- G>B | accept, keep your head low, and use the post to make the family's future safe | line: cross | v: security, tradition | act: accept, keep their head low, and use the post to make the family's future safe | chance: 80
works: The choice settles, and over the years people come to trust {Ns} word on things that matter.
works: Someone who once doubted {N} says, in passing, that {N} did the thing they could not have done.
fails: The cost turns out larger than {N} thought, and a door at work closes and stays closed.
fails: {N} lies awake going over it, and the promise comes back in the small hours.

